A||N||6||grinthock||Brake Question - Why does it do that?||||1||
Z||000000||grinthock||10-20-2001||10:42 AM||||I have a question.  I know how to do basic brake work, finished front pads this morn.<BR> <P>I have always had a question, <P>When you PUSH the brake when the car is off the pedal stiffens, then when you start it, it loosens off.  Why is this?  I thought that the pedal pushed the booster which pushes the master which pushes fluid around, no real mechanics involved just hydrolics.<P>Anyone got a better explanation?  Thanks guys/gals.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif"> </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||10-20-2001||11:03 AM||||The booster gives quite a bit of assist.  With the engine off, the vacuum assist goes away and you would have to exert a LOT more pressure on the pedal to get the same amount of travel.  If you were to drive the car with the booster unhooked from the vacuum, you would discover that even when the pedal is pushed down to the point that it feels solid, you wouldn't be slowing down very well.  All just a matter of mechanical advantage.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||grinthock||10-20-2001||11:19 AM||||So the booster is assisted by Vaccum?  where does it get the vac from?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodrv6||10-20-2001||01:18 PM||||The vacuum comes from the intake manifold on the engine--very long tube that runs under the console to the front of the car!<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000004||grinthock||10-20-2001||05:19 PM||||I guess it's just one of the things I havn't dealt with yet.  I looked in the book, I see that line, it goes near the gas tank.  Took a look to confirm my thoughts.  <P>Thanks for the help guys, a stupid question I know.||||reg||1
